Let $a=\vec{uv}$, $C$ be the set of weak proper $k$-colorings of $G$, and $C_a$ be the set of weak proper $k$-colorings of $G_a$. Therefore, $\chi_G(k) + \chi_{G_{a}}(k) = |C \cup C_a| + |C \cap C_a|$.

A coloring $c \in C \cup C_a$ if and only if $c$ is a weak proper $k$-coloring of $G-a$. A coloring $c \in C \cap C_a$ if and only if $c(u) = c(v)$ and $c$ corresponds to a weak proper $k$-coloring of $G/a$ in which the vertex created by identifying $u$ and $v$ is colored with $c(u)$. Therefore, $\chi_{G-a}(k) = |C \cup C_a|$ and $\chi_{G/a}(k) = |C \cap C_a|.$




\end{proof}

